# Rewrite Feature Extractor to Match UCI Phishing Dataset

The model was trained on the UCI Phishing Websites Dataset (30 binary features encoded as -1/0/1). The current [feature_extractor.py](file:///c:/Users/USER/Desktop/Phishing_Detector/phishing-detection-api/phishing-detection-api/app/feature_extractor.py) generates completely different continuous features, causing random predictions. This rewrite aligns inference features with training features.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **7 of 30 features** (domain age, registration length, web traffic, page rank, Google index, links pointing to page, statistical report) require external APIs (WHOIS, Alexa, Google) that are either paid or deprecated. These will default to **0 (suspicious/neutral)** for now, which is a safe middle-ground. The model still has 23 real features to work with — a massive improvement over the current state where **all 30 are wrong**.

---

## Proposed Changes

### Feature Extractor

#### [MODIFY] [feature_extractor.py](file:///c:/Users/USER/Desktop/Phishing_Detector/phishing-detection-api/phishing-detection-api/app/feature_extractor.py)

Complete rewrite to produce the **exact 30 UCI features** in order, with -1/0/1 encoding:

| # | Feature | Source | Encoding |
|---|---------|--------|----------|
| 0 | `having_IP_Address` | URL parsing | -1 if IP in URL, else 1 |
| 1 | `URL_Length` | `len(url)` | 1 if <54, 0 if 54-75, -1 if >75 |
| 2 | `Shortening_Service` | URL matching | -1 if shortened, else 1 |
| 3 | `having_At_Symbol` | URL parsing | -1 if @ present, else 1 |
| 4 | `double_slash_redirecting` | URL parsing | -1 if // after protocol, else 1 |
| 5 | `Prefix_Suffix` | Domain parsing | -1 if '-' in domain, else 1 |
| 6 | `having_Sub_Domain` | Domain parsing | 1 if ≤1 dot, 0 if 2, -1 if 3+ |
| 7 | `SSLfinal_State` | SSL check | 1 valid, 0 untrusted, -1 none |
| 8 | `Domain_registration_length` | ⚠️ Default 0 | Needs WHOIS |
| 9 | `Favicon` | HTML + domain check | -1 external, 1 same domain |
| 10 | `port` | URL parsing | -1 if non-standard, else 1 |
| 11 | `HTTPS_token` | Domain parsing | -1 if "https" in domain part, else 1 |
| 12 | `Request_URL` | HTML img/script/link src | -1 if >61% external, 0 if 22-61%, 1 if <22% |
| 13 | `URL_of_Anchor` | HTML anchor hrefs | -1 if >67% external, 0 if 31-67%, 1 if <31% |
| 14 | `Links_in_tags` | HTML meta/script/link tags | -1 if >81% external, 0 if 17-81%, 1 if <17% |
| 15 | `SFH` | HTML form action | -1 if blank/about:blank, 0 if foreign, 1 if same |
| 16 | `Submitting_to_email` | HTML form action | -1 if mailto:, else 1 |
| 17 | `Abnormal_URL` | WHOIS vs URL | ⚠️ Default 0 (needs WHOIS) |
| 18 | `Redirect` | HTTP response | 1 if ≤1 redirect, 0 if 2-3, -1 if ≥4 |
| 19 | `on_mouseover` | HTML content | -1 if statusbar change, else 1 |
| 20 | `RightClick` | HTML content | -1 if right-click disabled, else 1 |
| 21 | `popUpWidnow` | HTML content | -1 if popup with text field, else 1 |
| 22 | `Iframe` | HTML content | -1 if iframe present, else 1 |
| 23 | `age_of_domain` | ⚠️ Default 0 | Needs WHOIS |
| 24 | `DNSRecord` | DNS lookup | -1 if no record, else 1 |
| 25 | `web_traffic` | ⚠️ Default 0 | Alexa deprecated |
| 26 | `Page_Rank` | ⚠️ Default 0 | Google PR deprecated |
| 27 | `Google_Index` | ⚠️ Default 0 | Needs Google API |
| 28 | `Links_pointing_to_page` | ⚠️ Default 0 | Needs external data |
| 29 | `Statistical_report` | ⚠️ Default 0 | Needs PhishTank API |

**Key changes from current code:**
- Always fetch HTML (no keyword gating)
- All features encoded as -1/0/1 (not continuous values)
- Feature order matches UCI dataset exactly
- Graceful fallbacks with try/except (default 0 on failure)
- HTML fetch timeout stays at 2 seconds

---

## Verification Plan

### Manual Testing via API

No existing automated tests exist. Verification will be done by running the API locally and testing predictions:

1. Start the API server:
   ```
   cd c:\Users\USER\Desktop\Phishing_Detector\phishing-detection-api\phishing-detection-api
   python -m uvicorn app.main:app --reload --port 8000
   ```

2. Test with known safe URLs (expect "legitimate"):
   ```
   curl -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/predict -H "Content-Type: application/json" -d "{\"url\": \"https://www.google.com\"}"
   curl -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/predict -H "Content-Type: application/json" -d "{\"url\": \"https://www.github.com\"}"
   ```

3. Test with suspicious/phishing-like URLs (expect "phishing" or higher confidence):
   ```
   curl -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/predict -H "Content-Type: application/json" -d "{\"url\": \"http://192.168.1.1/login.html\"}"
   curl -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/predict -H "Content-Type: application/json" -d "{\"url\": \"http://g00gle-login-verify.tk/secure/update\"}"
   ```

4. Compare confidence values — safe URLs should show lower phishing probability than suspicious ones.
